From: DragonWarrior4NESRecomp
Subject: [PATCH] cyc_ui_imgui: scale the renderer for HiDPI before drawing the menu

Dear ImGui lays the runtime menu out in window units (points on macOS)
while the SDL renderer draws in pixels. imgui_impl_sdlrenderer2 expects the
caller to set SDL_RenderSetScale to the framebuffer ratio, as its SDL example
does; without it a Retina display (ratio 2) drew the menu at half size in the
top-left with clip rectangles scaled differently from the geometry, cutting
off its text. Set the scale around RenderDrawData and reset it before the
picture's logical size is restored. A ratio of 1 (Windows, Linux) is
unchanged.
---
diff --git a/runner/cyc/cyc_ui_imgui.cpp b/runner/cyc/cyc_ui_imgui.cpp
index 9d8b923..9e8c8f4 100644
--- a/runner/cyc/cyc_ui_imgui.cpp
+++ b/runner/cyc/cyc_ui_imgui.cpp
@@ -104,7 +104,17 @@ extern "C" void cyc_ui_render(void)
     recomp_runtime_ui_render_imgui(ui);
     cyc_state_ui_render();
     ImGui::Render();
+    // ImGui lays out in window units (points on macOS) while the renderer
+    // draws in pixels. As in ImGui's SDL_Renderer example, scale the renderer
+    // by the framebuffer ratio (2 on Retina, 1 elsewhere): the backend then
+    // keeps vertices and clip rectangles in the same units. Without it a
+    // Retina display drew the menu at half size with misplaced clipping.
+    {
+        const ImVec2 fb = ImGui::GetIO().DisplayFramebufferScale;
+        SDL_RenderSetScale(s_ren, fb.x > 0.0f ? fb.x : 1.0f, fb.y > 0.0f ? fb.y : 1.0f);
+    }
     ImGui_ImplSDLRenderer2_RenderDrawData(ImGui::GetDrawData(), s_ren);
+    SDL_RenderSetScale(s_ren, 1.0f, 1.0f);
     SDL_RenderSetLogicalSize(s_ren, lw, lh);
     SDL_RenderSetViewport(s_ren, &viewport);
     SDL_SetRenderDrawBlendMode(s_ren, SDL_BLENDMODE_NONE);
